    "note": "Complete individual Mariinskyi Palace exterior: mint-blue/cream two-story main palace, three projecting raised risalits/crowns, curved rear hall, shallow gray-blue hipped roofs and chimneys, attached low U wings and extended transverse end annexes. Real recessed glazing/closed portals, cream columns and original simplified curved ornament/open roof balustrades. Main forecourt and small rear service court stay roof-free. Independent Rada, administrative buildings, park and fountains remain native. No copied statues, heraldry, inscriptions, event furniture or interiors. Approximate198m standard global Terrarium reference and198.8m palace floor. Main eave10.3m, side-risalit eave12.1m and central-risalit eave13.2m above floor; low wings5.5m. Picture-guided roof/crown proportions and supported bounded entrance transitions, not surveyed historic thresholds. Only occupied palace and three small entry aprons receive ground openings; forecourt/park stay unchanged. +X NE along main palace range; -X SW toward independent Rada; +Z SE main U-shaped forecourt; -Z NW rear gardens. +Y up. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
